meta {
  name: Create Completeness Attribute - Real References (500, Bug)
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/product-attributes
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "wc_test_completeness_real",
    "type": "CompletenessAttribute",
    "attributes": [{"id": "6a9f1bf72b6fd055ffb7c7e1"}]
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 500
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 -- `USER_FLOWS.md` Flow 3. Creates nothing
  (server error).

  ## Real, reproducible bug -- blocks Flow 3 entirely
  `CompletenessAttribute.attributes` needs `[{"id": "..."}]` objects, not
  raw ID strings (confirmed via a 422 first --
  `RelatedAttributeDto` requires an object; matches
  `openapi_pimv3.json`'s schema). But once given the **correct** shape
  with a real attribute id, the request 500s:
  `{"data":[],"errors":[{"name":"ConfigurationError","description":
  "There was an error processing your request. Please try again later"}]}`.
  Reproduced twice, with both one and two real attribute references --
  consistent, not a fluke.

  This is a **different** failure category from `HierarchyAttribute`'s
  500 (`Create Attribute - HierarchyAttribute (500, Unimplemented).bru`)
  -- that's an undocumented/unimplemented type. `CompletenessAttribute`
  is a fully documented, spec'd type (Phase 1d smoke-tested it
  successfully with an **empty** `attributes` array) that breaks the
  moment it's given the real references the feature exists to use. Flag
  to Plytix as a live bug, not a documentation gap -- this blocks any
  docs about actually using Completeness Attributes for their intended
  purpose.
}
